From 803d976c6897b04bf3e29e7dbcff91f232902ba6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 23:28:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(app): every op that reads the setup's stock digests it in
 its stamp

The rapid-in-stock laws (#96, #106), the prior acquittal, the reach and
R-plane laws and the lathe meridian bar all read the setup's stock, but
only Drill's stamp digested it (#77/#91). Enlarging the stock after
generation left a Contour whose dive now lands in material reading Ok,
and the post let it through.

The stock reaches every generator through one seam (collect_job hands
every non-stock-sourced kind the stock's facets and box), so the set is
explicit: every op whose source is not the stock itself
(operation::reads_setup_stock). Its stamp now carries the stock term:
presence, placement, the mesh signature, and the shape's kind and
parameters. The stock-as-source arm moves to the new stamp_stock module
with its bytes unchanged, keeping stamp.rs under 400 lines.

Existing saved projects read their part-sourced ops Stale once and clear
on regenerate (the same one-time churn as earlier stamp moves).

Pinned by stock_stamp: enlarging the stock over a contour's dive stales
it and blocks the post; moving the stock stales it; undo returns Ok; a
work-material change stales nothing.

Fixes #156

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
